  "text": "Allergies:\nlisinopril\n\nChief Complaint:\nR ankle infection\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nMr. ___ is here for regularly\nscheduled postoperative visit approximately 12 weeks from the\ndate of surgery. He has been having a weeks worth of low grade\nfevers. He has been having wound care for his dorsal foot ulcer\nwhich resulted from skin necrosis prior to his original surgery\nand now has increased redness surrounding the ulcer.  He also \nhas\nbeen having wound care treatments with a silver sponge. He has\nrecently developed increased odor in the site as well.  He is\nconcerned about infection.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\nThe patient presented to the emergency department and was \nevaluated by the orthopedic surgery team. The patient was found \nto have R ankle cellulitis and was admitted to the orthopedic \nsurgery service. The patient was treated with IV vancomycin and \nelevation with improving. He was treated with BID Dakins WTD \ndressing changes. He had o a regular diet and oral medications \nwithout issue. The patient was given ppx anticoagulation per \nroutine. The patient's home medications were continued \nthroughout this hospitalization. The patient worked with ___ who \ndetermined that discharge to home was appropriate. The ___ \nhospital course was otherwise unremarkable.\n\nAt the time of discharge the patient's pain was well controlled, \nwound was nonpurulent, and the patient was voiding/moving bowels \nspontaneously. The patient is WBAT RLE in ACB, and will be \ndischarged on no chemical DVT prophylaxis. The patient will \nfollow up with Dr. ___ a wound check in a week, with Dr. \n___ in 3 months for repeat XRs. He will go out on \nBactrim/Keflex for a week with continued local wound care with \nDakins WTD BID. A thorough discussion was had with the patient \nregarding the diagnosis and expected post-discharge course \nincluding reasons to call the office or return to the hospital, \nand all questions were answered. The patient was also given \nwritten instructions concerning precautionary instructions and \nthe appropriate follow-up care. The patient expressed readiness \nfor discharge.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nR ankle cellulitis",
